course: dictionary
lesson: 1384
title: Capsize: when a boat turns over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To capsize means to turn over in the water so that the bottom of the boat is on top. You can also capsize a boat, which means to make it turn over. Read the clues around the word: it is a boat in water, so it is something that flips a boat over.
explain: «If a small boat capsizes, stay with the boat and hold on, and always wear a life jacket.» The words stay, hold on and life jacket tell you capsize is a danger, and what to do about it. Try your meaning in the sentence: "if a small boat turns over in the water..." still makes sense.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, «Mole grabs the oars, the boat capsizes, and the Rat has to pull him out of the river.» The boat is the thing that turns over, and Mole ends up in the water. Capsize is a verb, so it changes its ending: capsizes, capsized, capsizing.
fact: Capsize is a verb. Capsize, capsizes, capsized and capsizing are all forms of it.
fact: To capsize means to turn over in the water so that the bottom of the boat is on top.
fact: You can also capsize a boat, which means to make it turn over.
fact: «If a small boat capsizes, stay with the boat and hold on, and always wear a life jacket.» Staying with the boat keeps you safe until help comes.
fact: «"yú" (rising) means fish; ... some families never flip the fish over, like a boat capsizing.» Flipping a boat over and flipping a fish over are both turning something upside down.
exercise: «If a small boat capsizes, stay with the boat and hold on.» What should you do if a small boat capsizes? | Swim as fast as you can to the shore without it | *Stay with the boat and hold on | Shout and wave your arms at the sky | Let go and sink to the bottom
exercise: «The boat capsizes, and the Rat has to pull him out of the river.» What does capsizes mean here? | Sails very fast across the river | Gets a new coat of paint | Stops at the bank | *Turns over in the water
exercise: Which word is the past tense of capsize? | capsizing | capsizes | capsize | *capsized
test: What does «to make a boat capsize» mean? | To paint a boat bright red | To row a boat faster | To tie a boat to the dock | *To make a boat turn over
test: Which is the -ing form of capsize? | *capsizing | capsize | capsizes | capsized
exam: Which sentence uses capsize correctly? | Mole capsized his breakfast onto the table. | *When the big wave hit, the small boat capsized and tipped everyone into the sea. | We capsized the sunny afternoon with a picnic. | The cat capsized on the sofa to sleep.
